{#
  One real <table> per listing, with pagination, free-text search, and -- whenever rows carry a
  `data-category`/`data-mod` -- an auto-populated <select> filtering on it (hidden only if no row
  has a value for that dimension at all; a single distinct value still shows the dropdown, since
  that's what makes it start working immediately for free once a 2nd value appears). A 4th,
  separate filter dimension exists for tags specifically (`data-tags`, space-separated, exact-token
  match via the `?tag=` URL param rather than the free-text `?q=` substring search) -- it has no
  <select> of its own since there's no small fixed set of tags to populate one from; it renders as
  a removable chip only when a `tag` param is actually active (see datatable.js). All filters sync
  to URL query params (q/category/mod/tag, numbered q2/category2/mod2/tag2 etc for the 2nd+
  datatable on the same page) so a filtered view can be bookmarked/shared and survives
  back/forward navigation -- see datatable.js.
  Pass `headers` for the <thead> and have the caller emit
  <tr data-search="..." data-category="..." data-mod="..." data-tags="..."><td>...</td>...</tr>
  rows (any of the four data-* attributes can be omitted when not meaningful for that listing).
  When the caller produces zero rows, the whole widget (including any surrounding heading the page
  itself wraps around it) should be skipped by the page template -- this macro itself always
  renders the table shell since it doesn't know the row count up front.
  Every header is clickable to sort the (filtered) rows by that column's cell text (numeric-aware;
  click again to reverse, a 3rd click returns to unsorted) -- see datatable.js, no data-* opt-in
  needed, this applies to every datatable automatically.
#}
{% macro datatable(pageSize, placeholder, headers) %}
<div class="datatable" data-page-size="{{ pageSize or 50 }}">
  <div class="datatable-controls">
    <input type="search" class="datatable-search" placeholder="{{ placeholder or 'Search...' }}" aria-label="{{ placeholder or 'Search' }}">
    <select class="datatable-category-filter" aria-label="Filter by category"></select>
    <select class="datatable-mod-filter" aria-label="Filter by mod"></select>
  </div>
  <table>
    {% if headers %}<thead><tr>{% for h in headers %}<th class="datatable-sortable" data-col="{{ loop.index0 }}"><span class="datatable-th-label">{{ h | safe }}</span></th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>{% endif %}
    <tbody data-datatable-items>
      {{ caller() }}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="datatable-pagination" data-datatable-pagination></div>
</div>
{% endmacro %}
